{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/855890-dark-eras-for-us","id":855890,"title":"Dark Eras for us!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-30T12:35:42-07:00","id":855890,"title":"Dark Eras for us!","content":"So from Dark Eras Changeling has gotten:<br /> <br /> Three Kingdoms of Darkness (220-280)- Combo setting with Geist (2ed)<br /> -Directional Courts (4 Directions and Center)<br /> -6 new Directional Contracts<br /> <br /> Requiem for Regina (1593)- Add on to the vampire setting. (2ed)<br /> -Rose Courts (Blood, Snow, Ash)<br /> -3 new Contracts<br /> <br /> Lily, Sabre, and Thorn (1600s- early 1700s)- Pre-Revolutionary France (1ed)<br /> -Seasonal Courts<br /> -New Contract of Blades<br /> -3 new Tokens<br /> -New Entitlement: The Knights of St. Collen<br /> <br /> Grimm Dark Era (1812-1820)- German Fairy Tales (2ed)<br /> -Freehold of Golden Creation (Sciences, Arts)<br /> -4 new Trifles<br /> -4 new Tokens<br /> -6 new Contracts<br /> -Grimm Seeming<br /> -New Entitlement: Companions of the Resigned<br /> -New Entitlement: The Order of the Story Heroes<br /> <br /> So it's quite a bit! Thoughts, opinions, hopes, and dreams? I've already got a Grimm character I want to play now, and I wish Fabula Rasa still had their Elizabethan Lost game going...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:13:27-07:00","id":855928,"title":"","content":"I am going to be super busy just digesting everything that's happened for Changeling.<br /> <br /> By the way, that Grimm chapter? I'm gonna have to read it more closely, but I think it just introduced a major cosmological setting detail for Changeling, one that probably should call for a rewrite of most of the historical settings prior to it. But I need to actually read it to be sure.<br /> <br /> Good times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:42:50-07:00","id":855958,"title":"","content":"Well you can't just drop something on me like that while I'm on my phone at work without details! Details!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:55:31-07:00","id":855976,"title":"","content":"I can't give details because I haven't read it yet! I haven't even started Istanbul yet!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:11:21-07:00","id":855988,"title":"","content":"I really like the book. The fluff is really amazing and I love all the courts that has been added <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It seems to me that some of the changeling stuff in the book suffer from a lack of common nomenclature:<br /> - the Directional Courts from the Three Kingdoms of Darkness chapter lack a common bulwark, court contracts and court approachs ;<br /> - the Contracts of the Directional Courts from the Three Kingdoms of Darkness chapter possess strange dicepools associated with the level of mantle and who seem to be based with the first edition mindset of Skill/Attribute + Wyrd and not the Attribute + Skill + Wyrd of second edition ;<br /> - the Rose Courts from the Requiem for Regina chapter lack court contracts and court approachs ;<br /> - the Contracts of the Blade from the Lily, Sabre and Thorn chapter are first edition while the rest are second edition ;<br /> - the Contracts from the Grimm chapter lack the exceptional success section and seeming affinity. Also, their dicepools seem to be based with the first edition mindset of Skill/Attribute + Wyrd and not the Attribute + Skill + Wyrd of second edition ;<br /> - the Grimm seeming from the Grimm chapter lacks the non-Clarity bonus of his blessing who has been previewed.<br /> It's just plainly confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:16:40-07:00","id":855993,"title":"","content":"In the defense of London's Rose Courts, 5000 words is a lot less than you'd think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:25:03-07:00","id":856003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/855890-dark-eras-for-us?p=855976#post855976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't give details because I haven't read it yet! I haven't even started Istanbul yet!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, I'll be interested to hear your thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:27:09-07:00","id":856007,"title":"","content":"I may have skipped ahead to read about the Grimms...<br /> <br /> But yeah, that era is currently experiencing a &quot;story re-write&quot; of the Hedge and Arcadia. Previously, all the little towns in Germany have slightly different stories, meaning magic works slightly differently there (and going to a new town gives you a -1 to all magic stuff until you get acclimated). Then, the Bros Grimm published their book, and everyone started reading it. And in the towns where a lot of people read it, the Hedge and Arcadia started shifting, just a little, until it matched the stories that people were reading (or at least, better matched). The town goes through a month of Wyrd updates, where Contracts go haywire and Masks might drop for no reason, and then, it's fine, back to normal. But, between that town and any other town that experienced this, their magic is now same-y enough that there's not a penalty for traveling to and from those places. They have the same (enough) stories. All because of the power of literacy.<br /> <br /> Implications being, of course, that separate areas have separate stories, and traveling between them causes things to work just a bit differently. As places share stories (through books, newspapers, internet), they become more similar story-wise and Wyrd-wise. Meaning early eras may have had these variations through each town, but more modern ones share stories by state, nation, even globally. (Also means that, if stories get shared enough places, Arcadia will change to match. Slenderman was once just part of the internet, but he's popular enough that the Black-Suited Being can snatch you away to fairy-land now...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T15:55:24-07:00","id":856051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/855890-dark-eras-for-us?p=855993#post855993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the defense of London's Rose Courts, 5000 words is a lot less than you'd think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand, but for now it just seems for me that the writers were given different reference documents concerning the second edition and that they all applied what they knew about, which isn't the same chapter after chapter, and even inside the same era. It's feel rushed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T16:44:57-07:00","id":856075,"title":"","content":"With Approaches at least it's fairly simple to come up with thematic choices. I've never had the impression that the listed Approaches are the only Approaches a court has anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T17:14:36-07:00","id":856091,"title":"","content":"It's difficult to say since we don't have the second edition in our hands yet, so yes, no, maybe, but I really think they should have been implanted, especially after they were so stressed as important mechanics on these forums and on the previewed documents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:36:55-07:00","id":856406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/855890-dark-eras-for-us?p=855988#post855988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the book. The fluff is really amazing and I love all the courts that has been added <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It seems to me that some of the changeling stuff in the book suffer from a lack of common nomenclature:<br /> - the Directional Courts from the Three Kingdoms of Darkness chapter lack a common bulwark, court contracts and court approachs ;<br /> - the Contracts of the Directional Courts from the Three Kingdoms of Darkness chapter possess strange dicepools associated with the level of mantle and who seem to be based with the first edition mindset of Skill/Attribute + Wyrd and not the Attribute + Skill + Wyrd of second edition ;<br /> - the Rose Courts from the Requiem for Regina chapter lack court contracts and court approachs ;<br /> - the Contracts of the Blade from the Lily, Sabre and Thorn chapter are first edition while the rest are second edition ;<br /> - the Contracts from the Grimm chapter lack the exceptional success section and seeming affinity. Also, their dicepools seem to be based with the first edition mindset of Skill/Attribute + Wyrd and not the Attribute + Skill + Wyrd of second edition ;<br /> - the Grimm seeming from the Grimm chapter lacks the non-Clarity bonus of his blessing who has been previewed.<br /> It's just plainly confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div> You should copy paste this to the dark eras eratta thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:41:21-07:00","id":856409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/855890-dark-eras-for-us?p=856051#post856051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand, but for now it just seems for me that the writers were given different reference documents concerning the second edition and that they all applied what they knew about, which isn't the same chapter after chapter, and even inside the same era. It's feel rushed.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is all fixable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T07:42:21-07:00","id":856465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/855890-dark-eras-for-us?p=856007#post856007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have skipped ahead to read about the Grimms...<br /> <br /> But yeah, that era is currently experiencing a &quot;story re-write&quot; of the Hedge and Arcadia. Previously, all the little towns in Germany have slightly different stories, meaning magic works slightly differently there (and going to a new town gives you a -1 to all magic stuff until you get acclimated). Then, the Bros Grimm published their book, and everyone started reading it. And in the towns where a lot of people read it, the Hedge and Arcadia started shifting, just a little, until it matched the stories that people were reading (or at least, better matched). The town goes through a month of Wyrd updates, where Contracts go haywire and Masks might drop for no reason, and then, it's fine, back to normal. But, between that town and any other town that experienced this, their magic is now same-y enough that there's not a penalty for traveling to and from those places. They have the same (enough) stories. All because of the power of literacy.<br /> <br /> Implications being, of course, that separate areas have separate stories, and traveling between them causes things to work just a bit differently. As places share stories (through books, newspapers, internet), they become more similar story-wise and Wyrd-wise. Meaning early eras may have had these variations through each town, but more modern ones share stories by state, nation, even globally. (Also means that, if stories get shared enough places, Arcadia will change to match. Slenderman was once just part of the internet, but he's popular enough that the Black-Suited Being can snatch you away to fairy-land now...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder,maybe the modern gentry are even more brutal and gory than they were once because of game of thrones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T08:01:41-07:00","id":856479,"title":"","content":"Game of Thrones only wishes it was the horror stories told in encampments and trenches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T08:23:37-07:00","id":856492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/855890-dark-eras-for-us?p=856479#post856479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Game of Thrones only wishes it was the horror stories told in encampments and trenches.</div> </div> </div> </div>you fought on iraq?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T08:45:46-07:00","id":856504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/855890-dark-eras-for-us?p=856492#post856492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you fought on iraq?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell no! I'm reckless, but I'm not that reckless!<br /> <br /> But I've been around soldiers and veterans my entire life. I've grown up with stories of all sorts. And that's not even accounting for the gangland violence that I would stumble across as a kid. I saw my first dead body lying on the dirt of the side of the road about, what, seven? Think it was second grade.<br /> <br /> Point is, I'm not sure how much of a drop in the bucket Game of Thrones is. If anything, it's violence is tame.<br /> <br /> ...but it occurs me to me my barometer for that might be skewed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:23:42-07:00","id":856532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/855890-dark-eras-for-us?p=856504#post856504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell no! I'm reckless, but I'm not that reckless!<br /> <br /> But I've been around soldiers and veterans my entire life. I've grown up with stories of all sorts. And that's not even accounting for the gangland violence that I would stumble across as a kid. I saw my first dead body lying on the dirt of the side of the road about, what, seven? Think it was second grade.<br /> <br /> Point is, I'm not sure how much of a drop in the bucket Game of Thrones is. If anything, it's violence is tame.<br /> <br /> ...but it occurs me to me my barometer for that might be skewed.</div> </div> </div> </div>i'm sorry you saw that gruesome stuff outside of fiction man,if it ever happened to me i'd need a talk witha therapist,i admire your guts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:36:16-07:00","id":856580,"title":"","content":"Wow Arc, that sucks, no kid should group up like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T12:37:53-07:00","id":856654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/855890-dark-eras-for-us?p=855988#post855988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the book. The fluff is really amazing and I love all the courts that has been added <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It seems to me that some of the changeling stuff in the book suffer from a lack of common nomenclature:<br /> - the Directional Courts from the Three Kingdoms of Darkness chapter lack a common bulwark, court contracts and court approachs ;<br /> - the Contracts of the Directional Courts from the Three Kingdoms of Darkness chapter possess strange dicepools associated with the level of mantle and who seem to be based with the first edition mindset of Skill/Attribute + Wyrd and not the Attribute + Skill + Wyrd of second edition ;<br /> - the Rose Courts from the Requiem for Regina chapter lack court contracts and court approachs ;<br /> - the Contracts of the Blade from the Lily, Sabre and Thorn chapter are first edition while the rest are second edition ;<br /> - the Contracts from the Grimm chapter lack the exceptional success section and seeming affinity. Also, their dicepools seem to be based with the first edition mindset of Skill/Attribute + Wyrd and not the Attribute + Skill + Wyrd of second edition ;<br /> - the Grimm seeming from the Grimm chapter lacks the non-Clarity bonus of his blessing who has been previewed.<br /> It's just plainly confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought I recalled hearing that Dark Eras would be the last first edition material for Changeling, which would have been fitting and more easily accessible, since 2nd edition isn't finalized yet. It appears that that isn't the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":227,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","user":"KismetRose","date":". 03-31-2016, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T15:15:27-07:00","id":856742,"title":"","content":"The Lily, Sabre and Thorn chapter is clearly intended to be first edition, but it's not the same for the other ones who are clearly intended to work with the second edition:<br /> - Three Kingdoms of Darkness chapter: the courts are second edition (mention of goblin vow and a mantle intended to give bonus 1 to 5) and the contracts are second edition (they got seeming affinity) ;<br /> - Requiem for Regina chapter: the characters introduced are second edition (they have not the first edition spread of kith/seeming), the contracts are second edition (and perfectly in tune with the preview we got) and the courts are second edition (bulwark, goblin vow and a mantle intended to give bonus 1 to 5) ;<br /> - Grimm chapter: the courts are second edition (and use the correct rules we got previewed), the contracts are second edition (multiples references to Beats, Integrity &amp; Conditions) and the new Grimm seeming is clearly second edition.<br /> The problem that I have is that the mechanics of this three chapters are intended to work with the second edition of changeling, but they are not in check with the latest development. And what make it worse <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">(and feel like there was some kind of mistake that can be fixed) is that there are Contracts (the ones from Requiem for Regina) and Courts (from the Grimm chapter) that use the correct second edition rules that we know for now.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T16:02:09-07:00","id":856755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/855890-dark-eras-for-us?p=856742#post856742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lily, Sabre and Thorn chapter is clearly intended to be first edition, but it's not the same for the other ones who are clearly intended to work with the second edition:<br /> - Three Kingdoms of Darkness chapter: the courts are second edition (mention of goblin vow and a mantle intended to give bonus 1 to 5) and the contracts are second edition (they got seeming affinity) ;<br /> - Requiem for Regina chapter: the characters introduced are second edition (they have not the first edition spread of kith/seeming), the contracts are second edition (and perfectly in tune with the preview we got) and the courts are second edition (bulwark, goblin vow and a mantle intended to give bonus 1 to 5) ;<br /> - Grimm chapter: the courts are second edition (and use the correct rules we got previewed), the contracts are second edition (multiples references to Beats, Integrity &amp; Conditions) and the new Grimm seeming is clearly second edition.<br /> The problem that I have is that the mechanics of this three chapters are intended to work with the second edition of changeling, but they are not in check with the latest development. And what make it worse <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">(and feel like there was some kind of mistake that can be fixed) is that there are Contracts (the ones from Requiem for Regina) and Courts (from the Grimm chapter) that use the correct second edition rules that we know for now.</span></div> </div> </div> </div> This sounds like it should be fixible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T17:39:47-07:00","id":856798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/855890-dark-eras-for-us?p=856580#post856580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow Arc, that sucks, no kid should group up like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was an upper-middle class kid for the majority of my life. I actually had a good upbringing in a lot of ways. I also have a lot of shit in my baggage.<br /> <br /> Life's bittersweet for anyone. I know several who have had far more bitter lives than me. In the end, it turned out okay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T15:04:46-07:00","id":857305,"title":"","content":"I skipped ahead to A Grimm Dark Era for the new Seeming.<br /> <br /> But I stayed for the inspiration section's including Eraserhead and Hegel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:46:31-07:00","id":858034,"title":"","content":"I thought there was supposed to be a &quot;Loyalist&quot; seeming. Not complaining, just kinda bummed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T19:01:37-07:00","id":858075,"title":"","content":"The Loyalist Seeming is in the Core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base6