uote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/855890-dark-eras-for-us?p=860767#post860767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given that this is basically my mindset and I studied a combination of Roman/Islamic history, that statement gives me hope for my attempts at having a freelance career.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Fields of Interest are colonial North America and the intersection of gender and class. My research to this point has been on the commutation (or not) of execution sentences for pregnant women convicted of witchcraft in the seventeenth century.<br /> <br /> I won't give you shit history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T07:13:24-07:00","id":861018,"title":"","content":"Any chance you have interest in Mummy, too? That's a game big on history! I really am eager to get Dark eras once it comes out, and I like the extra material popping up on the forums. Perhaps if the writers have Seeming contracts in mind, I'm sure everyone here would be eager to see it, even if unofficial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T07:32:01-07:00","id":861025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/855890-dark-eras-for-us?p=861018#post861018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any chance you have interest in Mummy, too? That's a game big on history! I really am eager to get Dark eras once it comes out, and I like the extra material popping up on the forums. Perhaps if the writers have Seeming contracts in mind, I'm sure everyone here would be eager to see it, even if unofficial.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the game, but I wouldn't be best to write for it. I'm also not interested in Werewolf, neither game. Just not. We all have things we like and don't, I suppose.<br /> <br /> I wrote for the Grimm chapter--I said that above, but just repeating, since new people are coming--and for the Beast Dark Era. If you have any questions re: the Grim Dark Era, feel free to ask. If I don't know the answers, I'll funnel the questions to the other writers for the chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T22:30:52-07:00","id":864126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/855890-dark-eras-for-us?p=861025#post861025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have the game, but I wouldn't be best to write for it. I'm also not interested in Werewolf, neither game. Just not. We all have things we like and don't, I suppose.<br /> <br /> I wrote for the Grimm chapter--I said that above, but just repeating, since new people are coming--and for the Beast Dark Era. If you have any questions re: the Grim Dark Era, feel free to ask. If I don't know the answers, I'll funnel the questions to the other writers for the chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually doing some Grimm-related House Rules on my end, like what the missing facet of their Blessing could be (found in White Oak Dragon's Grimm FAQ) and some Grimm Contract clauses in a Contract conversion thread I have (found in my hub).<br /> <br /> One question. How do you imagine Grimm Seeming clauses working? Is it a lot like my approach to them? Or is it something else instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a